Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cpu-arm.c
Line: 427
Function: bfd_arm_update_notes
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: arch_string returned by arm_check_note points into the note descriptor but arm_check_note does not ensure a NUL terminator within buffer_size or that descsz is sufficient. A crafted note with a small (or zero) descsz and section size equal to the actual data can cause strcmp(arch_string, expected) to read past the end of the allocated buffer.

